      ],
      "explanation": "The leg opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle is half the hypotenuse, so \\(AB=2BC=8\\). Also, \\(AC=BC/\\tan 30^\\circ=4\\sqrt{3}\\).",
      "id": "thirty-degree-property-and-tangent",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_278_q1#thirty-degree-property-and-tangent",
      "title": "30° property and tangent"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_140",
        "cnm_174"
      ],
      "explanation": "Since \\(BC\\) is opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle in a right triangle, \\(AB=2BC=8\\). Once the hypotenuse is known, the Pythagorean theorem determines the other leg:\n\\[\nAC=\\sqrt{AB^2-BC^2}=\\sqrt{64-16}=4\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\nThus \\(AC=4\\sqrt{3}\\) and \\(AB=8\\), which is choice C.",
